#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110291 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4127f-1253-5aee-b524-84e5c6b2bc64" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Angles From Right, Straight, and Full Angles Using Algebra"}] :question/id #uuid "60df6f7a-5257-5081-ba0c-0e9499a15f23" :question/math-academy-id "e-10588" :question/problem "![](images/44/44aa56708e43f0518d7759e96b0770834f999998280c52910b2ca07cd607c1ab.png)\n\nGiven that $\\angle DOA$ is a straight angle, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\angle AOD$ is a straight angle and $\\angle BOC$ is a right angle. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOD={180}^{∘},\\,m∠BOC={90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB+m∠BOC+m∠COD & =m∠AOD \\\\ x+{90}^{∘}+(2x-{30}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 3x+{60}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={120}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110387 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d62f753-a3e0-5c7e-919d-3f878c1d8e93" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of Unknown Angles on a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "826ef015-53ba-5889-8749-170a656c35f9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2590" :question/problem "In the figure shown below, determine the measure of $\\angle EOA.$\n\n![](images/80/80f47745a289bf021a4566a58d1961c93bb216e2df900b8effae8f2dda3f1606.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, $\\angle COD$ is a right angle, so\n\n$$\nm\\angle COD = 90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nAlso, since $\\angle COD$ and $\\angle EOB$ are vertical angles, they have the same measure:\n\n$$\nm\\angle EOB=m\\angle COD=90^\\circ\n$$\n\nNow, since we know that $m\\angle AOB=40^{\\circ}$ and $m\\angle EOB = 90^\\circ,$ we can use the angle addition postulate to solve for $m\\angle EOA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠EOA+m∠AOB & =m∠EOB \\\\ m∠EOA+{40}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠EOA & ={50}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f64be210-e966-5be7-b7b4-cbf859793e76" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Angle Types From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "6438b232-f40a-54b0-a599-a1d6aa4151d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-2599" :question/problem "![](images/80/800f11f555f0c2be0e89aa26602cfe4a35a62f4fe2309dfe2a188f47138fb98b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above. Which of the following statements is true?\n\nI. $\\angle A$ is obtuse\n\nII. $\\angle B$ is a right angle\n\nIII. $\\angle A$ and $\\angle B$ are vertical angles" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the diagram, $\\angle A$ and the angle with measure $130^\\circ$ are vertical angles. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm\\angle A = 130^\\circ >    90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\angle A$ is an obtuse angle.\n\n- Statement II is false. From the diagram, $\\angle B$ and the angle with measure $50^\\circ$ are vertical angles. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm\\angle B = 50^\\circ \\neq    90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\angle B$ is not a right angle.\n\n- Statement III is false. Angles $\\angle A$ and $\\angle B$  are not vertical since they have a common side.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fea607a9-7512-5062-b4ae-c53e0f653efd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Angle Type From a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "15470df7-8d18-5427-9488-f3f10df13952" :question/math-academy-id "e-2601" :question/problem "Let $\\angle S$ and $\\angle T$ be two adjacent angles. Given that $\\angle S$ is a straight angle and $\\angle T$ is right, what type of angle is their sum?" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\angle S$ is a straight angle, we have\n\n$$\nm\\angle S=180^\\circ,\n$$\n\nand since $\\angle T$ is a right angle, we have \n\n$$\nm\\angle T=90^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nSo, their sum is \n\n$$\nm\\angle S + m\\angle T=180^{\\circ} + 90^{\\circ}=270^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the sum of $\\angle S$ and $\\angle T$ is a reflex angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fea607a9-7512-5062-b4ae-c53e0f653efd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Angle Type From a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ab0cf8-3f34-59c0-8e21-66edfaf04089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Full" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493460} {:answer/id #uuid "3e34a591-6a79-58e5-8bf2-b28cbeb7a5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Obtuse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493497} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2ca949-167e-5ea3-8f87-0bd5403b151a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflex" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493531} {:answer/id #uuid "78ed045b-f25b-5f3b-9f9b-72d9de4e2108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Right" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493574} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf6b57f-13bc-5f45-a7b4-af650da0ae8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Straight" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cf6b57f-13bc-5f45-a7b4-af650da0ae8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Straight" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493583} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8676a48-f37e-575d-b431-78b2e10570aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be894050-f250-5773-8720-f2e3adc2c8cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-118297" :question/problem "Let $∠N$ and $∠S$ be two adjacent angles. Given that $∠N$ is a null angle and $∠S$ is straight, what type of angle is their sum?" :question/worked-solution "Since $∠N$ is a null and a right angle, we have\n\n$$\nm∠N={0}^{∘}\n$$\n\nand since $∠S$ is a straight angle, we have\n\n$$\nm∠S={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, their sum is \n\n$$\nm∠N+m∠S={0}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the sum of $∠N$ and $∠S$ is a straight angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d62f753-a3e0-5c7e-919d-3f878c1d8e93" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of Unknown Angles on a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbfb00a3-d7b9-5630-b87d-050558a3b0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbfb00a3-d7b9-5630-b87d-050558a3b0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493699} :answer-field/id #uuid "40413315-c578-5bd8-a689-73bf0674b2fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7352f5cb-3930-54b5-bef8-2eba5dc04e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-171812" :question/problem "![](images/be/be311b9b624fba745b93d7ac3cd67ace3bbe4ea0650b12fa900d3aac50b5bae2.png)\n\nIn the figure shown above, the measure of $∠COF$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠EOD & =m∠EOB+m∠BOD \\\\  & ={82}^{∘}+{47}^{∘} \\\\  & ={129}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, $∠AOF$ and $∠EOD$ are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, we have \n\n$$\nm∠AOF=m∠EOD={129}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since $∠AOC$ is a right angle, the angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOF & =m∠AOC+m∠COF \\\\ {129}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+m∠COF \\\\ m∠COF & ={39}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4127f-1253-5aee-b524-84e5c6b2bc64" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Angles From Right, Straight, and Full Angles Using Algebra"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02975f11-2d2d-5929-8588-5012e8b84c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493394} {:answer/id #uuid "57826d32-8995-54d3-b84a-ec44c68faf1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493525} {:answer/id #uuid "6d96124d-f237-5464-9fe0-f5821f8ccf68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493552} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bf48eb-6be6-56cd-b586-74274b956554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493708} {:answer/id #uuid "c928eb56-fbb8-5dc6-b810-b590302de8de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d96124d-f237-5464-9fe0-f5821f8ccf68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493552} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ec9975b-d6f8-5646-b0e0-edaca8358321" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b151647b-d6b1-5228-a002-474a2ce605db" :question/math-academy-id "q-52647" :question/problem "![](images/a5/a5752cefaad576ffeb18408db80dac554a525a0e4137b46377fee225436da433.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $∠AOB≅∠COD$ and $∠BOC≅∠DOE.$ Given that $m∠AOB=2m∠BOC$ and that $∠AOE$ is a straight angle, $m∠BOC=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $∠AOB≅∠COD$ and $∠DOE≅∠BOC,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠COD \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since $∠AOE$ is a straight angle, we have $m∠AOE={180}^{∘}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB+m∠BOC+m∠COD+m∠DOE & =m∠AOE \\\\ m∠AOB+m∠BOC+m∠AOB+m∠BOC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠BOC+m∠BOC+2m∠BOC+m∠BOC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 6m∠BOC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠BOC & ={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d62f753-a3e0-5c7e-919d-3f878c1d8e93" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of Unknown Angles on a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2086e39b-cf43-5217-9c01-57d002497a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493446} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0b9a45-f419-5238-94d4-94c1a2452f82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493719} {:answer/id #uuid "e57e86ef-8464-506b-b83e-b486bc299195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493757} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e9243e-ffd6-5efc-991d-1dcba24e6b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493765} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d1d50a-79d8-5dd9-91c7-92b34f96b05a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2086e39b-cf43-5217-9c01-57d002497a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493446} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6cc1ff-d18a-5058-b987-d452bdea6e0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c27c7256-8071-50ae-b777-2aae5eb73a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-52734" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1fab2b2158183c89fb48259408e3a1c684af657cd34d68d4b79e4773a4251f37.png)\n\nIn the figure shown above, determine the measure of $∠GOH$ given that $m∠BOD={120}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, $∠AOC$ and $∠EOG$ are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, we have\n\n$$\nm∠AOC=m∠EOG={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since $∠AOC$ is a right angle, the angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB+m∠BOC & =m∠AOC \\\\ {30}^{∘}+m∠BOC & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠BOC & ={60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, given that $m∠BOD={120}^{∘}$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOC+m∠COD & =m∠BOD \\\\ {60}^{∘}+m∠COD & ={120}^{∘} \\\\ m∠COD & ={60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∠COD$ and $∠GOH$ are vertical angles. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠GOH=m∠COD={60}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493894 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f64be210-e966-5be7-b7b4-cbf859793e76" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Angle Types From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f35d0a0-72de-5c1b-8fef-a7aa761262ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493444} {:answer/id #uuid "32286793-c28f-5862-a676-dfdcef594030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493476} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe50095-7958-5765-aef7-914d268ee8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493500} {:answer/id #uuid "80cf6eca-cd51-5611-a089-8312085b8c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493593} {:answer/id #uuid "8a84c6f1-4efc-5f12-acaa-6660ac2f2a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fe50095-7958-5765-aef7-914d268ee8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493500} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9fbb57-14ec-5a87-a6ae-af2fa3a7feb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bd5f670-a4a8-511a-9fe4-89d9e2250371" :question/math-academy-id "q-52736" :question/problem "![](images/ae/aec20235a2968f30f1ac3861d429a4102464a701fff0a90c13dae97334735273.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above. Which of the following statements is true?\n\nI. $∠A$ is null\n\nII. $∠B$ is acute\n\nIII. $∠C$ is obtuse" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the diagram, it follows that $m∠A={180}^{∘}>{0}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement II is true, and statement III is false. Indeed, from the graph we deduce  that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠B+{100}^{∘}+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+m∠C & ={80}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of each of the angles $∠B$ and $∠C$ is less than ${80}^{∘},$ so these angles are acute angles.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fea607a9-7512-5062-b4ae-c53e0f653efd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Angle Type From a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c479774-aa4a-5084-a50f-b935229aed16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Acute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493411} {:answer/id #uuid "a973a754-84a1-5793-8718-0ba38046f99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Obtuse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493656} {:answer/id #uuid "b3842f72-fd00-53f0-8fc3-139197c1f664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflex" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493681} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb9aa9e-8ced-5049-8416-7993780d0987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Straight" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493707} {:answer/id #uuid "eeef453f-c7fd-5acd-9659-9446f38f849b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Full" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3842f72-fd00-53f0-8fc3-139197c1f664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflex" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493681} :answer-field/id #uuid "e85777c4-f5a5-5556-baa2-3cf1a0f7f89c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b814d590-16e2-55cf-89ba-ea5367397c7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-52745" :question/problem "Let $∠S$ and $∠T$ be two adjacent angles. Given that $∠S$ is a straight angle and $∠T$ is obtuse, what type of angle is their sum?" :question/worked-solution "Since $∠S$ is a straight angle, we have \n\n$$\nm∠S={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n Since $∠T$ is obtuse, we have\n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}<m∠T<{180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of these two angles satisfies by the following inequalies:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & <m∠S+m∠T<{180}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\ {270}^{∘} & <m∠S+m∠T<{360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the sum of $∠S$ and $∠T$ is a reflex angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4127f-1253-5aee-b524-84e5c6b2bc64" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Angles From Right, Straight, and Full Angles Using Algebra"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "409f8837-a9cd-5b82-a2d7-a206faa30f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493501} {:answer/id #uuid "698dc0ce-e75a-5496-830d-7bb5cb3e368e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493548} {:answer/id #uuid "713314d9-62ce-573b-96ab-e10c6a7069d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493559} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7d0d7c-0d46-5f63-ac35-435f9bfd536b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493612} {:answer/id #uuid "96cae35a-e83c-5482-a7dc-0a00c6cae34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "713314d9-62ce-573b-96ab-e10c6a7069d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493559} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a96b7f7-43ca-537f-a8b8-336694a0d953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6c23b91-4fda-5c9a-8297-f36bd4ddd1a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-53173" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d607ba743afcc7d39299278e0d352e2c644b587480834a5c68cf2b46687b7f73.png)\n\nWhat is the value of $t$ given that $∠VOZ$ is a right angle?" :question/worked-solution "Since $∠VOZ$ is a right angle, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠VOZ={90}^{∘},\\,m∠VOW=m∠YOZ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can form an equation and solve for $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠VOW+m∠WOX+m∠XOY+m∠YOZ & =m∠VOZ \\\\ {30}^{∘}+t+t+{30}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 2t & ={30}^{∘} \\\\ t & ={15}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f64be210-e966-5be7-b7b4-cbf859793e76" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Angle Types From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bdfb115-f1cf-595c-b0a6-1d8a5caa3a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493493} {:answer/id #uuid "9038dbdd-8eae-5460-b48d-1f1d998e1a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493620} {:answer/id #uuid "b143655e-9c66-5750-b57b-9f00bc54e9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493678} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa1faed-e1c5-57b8-a670-8810e5610649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493721} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc42be0-d433-5c09-92d2-0ad1be46916f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfa1faed-e1c5-57b8-a670-8810e5610649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493721} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec0276f1-96e6-52f4-9303-7a2cc6a4348f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "679aea70-862a-57d5-bcef-459256cb248c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76777" :question/problem "![](images/64/64fcf64e043698366083e24b6041e2fb406b725671ab71c0c871c7e708517685.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above. Which of the following statements is true?\n\nI. $∠A$ is a null angle\n\nII. $∠C$ is a full angle\n\nIII. $∠D$ is a right angle" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the diagram, $m∠A>{0}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the diagram, $m∠C<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. From the diagram, $m∠D={90}^{∘}.$ Therefore, $∠D$ is a right angle.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}]}
